//////////////////////// QUESTION ////////////////////////////

Delete kth node from a Circular Linked List

Input : [1|.]─►[2|.]─►[3|.]─►[4|.]─►(back to 1), k=3  
Output: [1|.]─►[3|.]─►[4|.]─►(back to 1)

Edge Cases:
1. head==null        →  return null
2. single node, k=1  →  return null
3. single node, k!=1 →  return head
4. k=1               →  traverse to last, point to head.next
5. k=last            →  swap with prev node, unlink

Constraints:
1 ≤ number of nodes ≤ 10⁵  
0 ≤ node.data ≤ 10⁵  
1 ≤ k ≤ number of nodes  

Sample Input 1 : k=3  
[1|.]─►[2|.]─►[3|.]─►[4|.]─►(back to 1)

Sample Output 1:  
[1|.]─►[3|.]─►[4|.]─►(back to 1)

Sample Input 2 : k=1  
[1|.]─►[2|.]─►(back to 1)

Sample Output 2:  
[2|.]─►(back to 2)

Sample Input 3 : single node, k=1  
[5|.]─►(back to 5)

Sample Output 3:  
null
